docs/WORKSPACE_BRIDGE_V1.md:76:a question, PR review, approval gate, or some other domain-specific workflow.
docs/WORKSPACE_BRIDGE_V1.md:80:`@hachej/boring-ask-user/server` owns the `ask-user.v1.*` operation family. Normal ask-user setup contributes those handlers through `workspaceBridgeHandlers` instead of registering a plugin-owned `/api/v1/questions/commands` route.
docs/WORKSPACE_BRIDGE_V1.md:84:- `ask-user.v1.request` — runtime/server asks a blocking structured question.
docs/WORKSPACE_BRIDGE_V1.md:85:- `ask-user.v1.pending` — browser/server reads the pending question for a session.
docs/WORKSPACE_BRIDGE_V1.md:86:- `ask-user.v1.answer` — browser/server submits answers with the question answer token and idempotency key.
docs/WORKSPACE_BRIDGE_V1.md:87:- `ask-user.v1.cancel` — browser/server cancels a pending question with the question answer token and idempotency key.
docs/WORKSPACE_BRIDGE_V1.md:90:The plugin owns question validation, storage, answer-token checks, UI-state publishing, and pending-question coordination. The workspace package remains domain-neutral: it hosts only the generic RPC core, the trusted handler contribution seam, and generic session attention/surface dispatch.
docs/WORKSPACE_BRIDGE_V1.md:92:For normal setup, browser reads/mutations are scoped by the verified bridge session (`x-boring-session-id` or app-auth equivalent), not by body-only session values. Runtime requests must be made with a session-scoped bridge token when a session id is present. UI effects and UI state may carry question/session hints for navigation and badges, but answer tokens and full answerable question payloads stay behind the `ask-user.v1.pending` RPC read.
