docs/issues/873/plan.md:10:# gh-873 CLI ask_user question should appear without page refresh
docs/issues/873/plan.md:14:In CLI workspace mode, an `ask_user` question can be pending while the already-open workspace Questions surface remains empty until the user refreshes the page.
docs/issues/873/plan.md:16:Clarified report: the user has repeatedly had to refresh the page to see an ask-user question; the workspace was open, but the Questions area/list was still empty.
docs/issues/873/plan.md:20:Investigate and fix the live update path from CLI ask-user server state to the front-end Questions UI. The fix should ensure that when a new pending question is created, an already-mounted CLI workspace receives the pending hint/state and opens or hydrates the question without page refresh.
docs/issues/873/plan.md:33:- Start with a failing no-refresh reproduction test that creates a pending question after the workspace is already mounted.
docs/issues/873/plan.md:43:- Highest public seam: ask-user plugin e2e/integration where a pending question is created after the page is already mounted and then appears without reload.
docs/issues/873/plan.md:50:- Clicking the existing Questions/open icon after the prompt arrives shows the pending question without refreshing the page.
docs/issues/873/plan.md:52:- Hidden-session/multi-session question behavior remains intact.
docs/issues/873/plan.md:57:- Screenshot/demo: question appears in the open Questions pane after triggering a CLI `ask_user` request.
docs/issues/873/plan.md:58:- Manual steps: open CLI workspace, trigger `ask_user`, do not refresh, verify the question appears.
docs/issues/873/plan.md:78:- Ask-user front tests already cover rehydrating pending questions after provider remount/refresh.
docs/issues/873/plan.md:86:- Resolved UX trigger: do not auto-open; update badge/attention state and ensure the existing open icon/pane hydrates the pending question without refresh.
docs/issues/873/plan.md:89:- **Concurrency:** multiple sessions/questions may race; fixing active-session only could regress hidden-session pending questions.
docs/issues/873/plan.md:94:**Resolved decision:** Do not auto-open/focus. Show a clear badge/attention indicator, and make the existing Questions/open icon hydrate/show the pending question without page refresh.
docs/issues/873/plan.md:96:**Evidence:** Current report says the workspace was open but empty; user clarified the question was not auto-opened and the open icon also failed, suggesting stale live state rather than an intentional focus behavior gap.
