/tmp/claude-1000/-home-ubuntu-projects-boring-ui-v2/2f6c6143-73be-4a87-886b-e8dd7fb126e0/scratchpad/research/r8-think.md:115:But the method call crosses Workers RPC into the host runtime. The host decides whether to replay, execute, or pause. Source: https://developers.cloudflare.com/agents/tools/codemode/api-reference/
/tmp/claude-1000/-home-ubuntu-projects-boring-ui-v2/2f6c6143-73be-4a87-886b-e8dd7fb126e0/scratchpad/research/r8-think.md:117:The generated code runs inside a fresh Dynamic Worker. `DynamicWorkerExecutor` is configured with a Worker Loader binding. The default timeout is 60,000 ms. The default `globalOutbound` is `null`. Therefore ordinary external `fetch()` and `connect()` are blocked by default. The sandbox calls connectors through an RPC dispatcher. At an approval-required connector method:
