docs/issues/391/runtime-refactor/work/S1-slack-channel/CHAN-A-chat-sdk-transport.md:19:v1→v2: 1 followUp :237 enqueues only. 2 double-start→atomic create. 3 A-2 REVERSED→one package. 4 D-RATIFY. 5 clientSeq required (:9-10). 6 ensureBridge (:140). 7 reject missing sessionId. 8 SDK content-store guard. 9 golden-run+shape spy. 10 secret guard. 11 ephemeral approvals (chat:1217). 12 native-streaming prereqs (index.js:3469). 13 dropped false core-dir. 14 appendToList :1138.
docs/issues/391/runtime-refactor/work/S1-slack-channel/CHAN-A-chat-sdk-transport.md:35:The Chat SDK owns ONLY per-platform transport + native rendering. boring-agent owns ALL conversation state: message list/transcript, sessions, durable replayable event stream, follow-up queue, approvals. The bridge is a pure forwarder — every inbound event maps to a facade call (agent.start/agent.followUp/agent.resolveInput) keyed by sessionId only; every render projected from agent.stream(...). The SDK StateAdapter holds transport plumbing ONLY (dedupe keys, lock tokens, subscription flags; installation storage forbidden or encryptionKey-gated); never conversation content; AND the Chat config never enables an SDK content store (transcripts/threadHistory/messageHistory/identity/persistThreadHistory). conversationKey→sessionId lives OUTSIDE the SDK, in host state.
docs/issues/391/runtime-refactor/work/S1-slack-channel/CHAN-A-chat-sdk-transport.md:47:Bridge data-flow (v6): Slack event →(@chat-adapter/slack webhook/socket)→ Chat(bot)[concurrency:'concurrent', single-writer §b2]. Inbound (mention/message converge): key=conversationKey(thread)=thread.id[spike:57]; {record,created,receipt}=sessions.getOrCreateSession(key,{allocate,admit}) — **owner-token-CAS reserve→allocate-before-admit→ready (BCH-003): winner CAS-reserves {creating,owner}, allocates a session ({admitting,sessionId,startIndex:0} CAS-persisted BEFORE prompt), admits via agent.start({sessionId,content}), CAS-writes {ready}; a stalled winner reclaimed past TTL fails its CAS and aborts; losers WAIT on an unexpired {creating|admitting} until {ready}, reclaim ONLY an expired record**. If created→admit(receipt.startIndex); else (pre-existing/recovered/lost-race)→agent.followUp(input) enqueued IMMEDIATELY (BCH-001 DrainCoordinator; single drain owner incl interrupt), then admit from the WINNER's record.startIndex (loser, no pump) / follow-up receipt.startIndex, with the idle-tail successor rule. onAction→resolveInput; T1-STUB: ephemeral "approvals not supported yet" (chat:1217). agent.stream(sessionId,{startIndex})→AsyncIterable<AgentEvent>(message-delta piChatEvent.ts:22)→thread.post(textDeltasUntilIdle(events))[spike:130; chat:1440+:1735]→@chat-adapter/slack chatStream+streamer.append[slack index.js:3431-3452].
docs/issues/391/runtime-refactor/work/S1-slack-channel/CHAN-A-chat-sdk-transport.md:79:    (C) cur is 'admitting' and EXPIRED (winner crashed mid-admit; sessionId EXISTS) → RECOVER: casState(key, expectedOwner:cur.owner, {state:'ready',sessionId:cur.sessionId,startIndex:cur.startIndex,agentId:cur.agentId}). if true → return {record:{sessionId:cur.sessionId,startIndex:cur.startIndex}, created:false} (recovered; the session is NOT re-allocated and NOT re-admitted — the caller sends its message as a follow-up; whether the crashed prompt produced partial output is a stream/runtime question needing integration testing). if false → owner changed, re-loop.
docs/issues/391/runtime-refactor/work/S1-slack-channel/CHAN-A-chat-sdk-transport.md:106:  onAction — agent.resolveInput(sessionId,event.actionId,{content:event.value,value:{…}}); on T1-stub (createAgent.ts:171-173): event.thread?.postEphemeral(event.user,"Approvals aren't supported yet.",{...}) (chat:1217); no fabricated approvals. input.originSurface default 'slack' (S3:101). input.ctx from optional host resolveContext; if absent omit — NEVER synthesize workspaceId (P1:29,:62; 08:217). src/bridge/streamToThread.ts — textDeltasUntilIdle reducer verbatim from spike:129-259; TEXT ONLY (finding 11-v2). __tests__.
docs/issues/391/runtime-refactor/work/S1-slack-channel/CHAN-A-chat-sdk-transport.md:122:1 No SDK-owned conversation state — never the message list, sessions, durable stream, follow-up queue, or any content store (transcripts/threadHistory/messageHistory/identity/persistThreadHistory). 2 No SDK queue/debounce/burst — concurrency:'concurrent' only (guarded). 3 No @chat-adapter/state-* — our ChatTransportStateAdapter is the only StateAdapter (guarded); the owner-CAS lives on OUR ConversationSessionStore backing, not the SDK adapter. 4 No live action resolution before T1, no approval buttons — resolveInput throws ERR_NOT_IMPLEMENTED_UNTIL_T1 (createAgent.ts:171-173); ephemeral "not supported yet" (finding 11-v2), text-only render. 5 No full multi-platform build — Slack first (Discord/etc + shared-core extraction = 2nd-adapter bead per D-RATIFY-2; T2:43). 6 No new shared/core package this pass — everything in packages/channels/slack; no pi-internal reach (public facade + @hachej/boring-agent/shared types only; 08:254, WORKSPACE_CONTRACT:1-4). Scoped exception: BCH-001's DrainCoordinator lives inside @hachej/boring-agent (HarnessPiChatService) — core follow-up/run orchestration. 7 No new event protocol / render-layer rewrite (reuse AgentEvent/PiChatEvent 08:139-156,:275). 8 No durable historical-replay dependency (live-tail from startIndex P1:117). 9 No horizontal scale beyond one bridge process per conversation this pass — single-writer (§b2) is enforced; the durable pump lease for multi-replica-per-conversation is a deferred follow-up.
